// ND 4.2 interface integration targets. Each is a role target run through
// run_integration_module.yaml (like INTEGRATION_MODULES) via include_role, so its
// vars/main.yaml auto-loads. They use their OWN nd_test_* variable namespace, so the
// shell loop injects nd_test_fabric_name + nd_test_switch_ip (and the parent/member
// overrides each needs). These targets always run (non-optional): they are appended to
// the run AND the result parser unconditionally, so the lab must keep the nd_interface_*
// substrate provisioned or the tests fail on a missing test-output file.
// Per-target prerequisites (NO cabling for any of the first nine below):
//   - loopback / svi                 : logical only; need just the target switch present.
//   - ethernet_access / trunk_host   : need free physical ports Eth1/41-1/50 on the switch
//                                      (must exist + NOT be port-channel members).
//   - ethernet_routed                : needs free routed-capable ports Eth1/31-1/34
//                                      (must exist + NOT be port-channel members).
//   - port_channel_access/trunk_host : need free member ports Eth1/10-1/13 (not in a PC).
//   - subinterface_managed/unmanaged : the prerequisite lifecycle verifies the existing leaf_1 Eth1/1 <->
//                                      external_edge_1 Eth1/1 cable (module is SKIP if it is absent),
//                                      creates a temporary routed Eth1/1 + memberless L3 Port-channel10
//                                      parent when absent, journals them, and restores the pre-test
//                                      state after target cleanup.
//   - vpc_access / vpc_trunk_host    : need the leaf_1 Eth1/2 <-> leaf_2 Eth1/1 peer-link cable and the leaf_3 <-> leaf_4
//                                      Eth1/1 + Eth1/2 peer-link cables, and free member ports on ALL FOUR leaves
//                                      (Eth1/5-1/7 + 1/10 access, Eth1/8-1/10 trunk-host). The runner forms the PHYSICAL
//                                      leaf pairs around the target (the target's own virtual-peer-link pair is rejected by
//                                      ND 4.3 on this fabric) and unpairs them afterwards. The targets' multi-pair scenario
//                                      asserts the leaf_3/leaf_4 pair as its SECOND reciprocal vPC pair
//                                      (nd_test_vpc_pair2_peer*_ip = 192.0.2.85/.86) and Eth1/10 (Eth1/9 for trunk-host)
